    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d441">

                <pb facs="0382" n="370" xml:id="pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.7962/67: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-18T22:00:00-00:44">March 18, 1942—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 19—2:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>88. From McBride. Department’s 52, March 13, 4 p.m. Am deeply concerned at delay
                    in approval of agreement. Our position is weakening daily here due to increased
                    submarine activity, two ships having been sunk off Liberian coast within a week,
                    one of them within sight of Cape Palmas, and to Department’s instruction to
                    evacuate American nationals.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d441-f1"/> Liberian
                    Government now so anxious about situation that I am afraid difficulty may be met
                    in proceeding with agreement here unless it is forthcoming immediately. Strongly
                    recommend it be approved in present form. Any changes that may be desired could
                    be incorporated in a subsequent amendment. [McBride.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
